  description="How durbeen.io handles information about you: no accounts, no cookies, one privacy-friendly analytics script. What the site stores and what its host can see."
>
  <p>This page explains what durbeen.io does with information about you. In short: very little.</p>

  <h2>What the website stores</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>There are no accounts or comments, and no forms that collect personal information (the search box runs only in your browser). The site does not ask for your name or email address.</li>
    <li>Durbeen sets no cookies.</li>
    <li>If you choose light or dark mode, that choice is saved in your browser's local storage, on your own device. It is never sent to Durbeen.</li>
    <li>
      Fonts come from durbeen.io itself, not from Google or another font service.
      The only third-party script is Cloudflare Web Analytics (see Analytics below).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the host can see</h2>
  <p>
    The site is hosted by Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare handles the technical data needed to deliver pages,
    such as your IP address and browser type, and may keep it in logs. See{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>Search</h2>
  <p>Search runs in your browser. Durbeen does not store what you search for.</p>

  <h2>Analytics</h2>
  <p>
    Durbeen uses Cloudflare Web Analytics to count page views and measure page speed. It does not use cookies and does
    not track you across other sites. See{' '}
    <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/privacypolicy/" rel="noopener">Cloudflare's privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>If you write to me</h2>
  <p>
    If you email <a href="mailto:hello@durbeen.io">hello@durbeen.io</a>, I receive your email address and your message. I use them to reply, and keep the
    email for as long as the conversation needs it. Email to this address is forwarded by Cloudflare Email Routing to my
    Google (Gmail) inbox, so Cloudflare and Google process it.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    The share buttons open LinkedIn or X only when you click them, and only with the address of the article. Those
    sites have their own privacy policies.
  </p>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    Under the law of India, and depending on where you live, you may have rights over information about you, such as seeing it, correcting it or
    asking for it to be deleted. Write to <a href="mailto:hello@durbeen.io">hello@durbeen.io</a>. The law that applies to this site is the law of India.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>I will change this page when what the site does changes, and update the date at the top.</p>
</LegalLayout>
